# google-services.json / GoogleService-Info.plist are deliberately tracked, not
# ignored — they're client-side Firebase config (project ID + a domain-restricted API
# key), not secrets, and EAS Build's project archive is built from what git tracks. An
# ignored copy here is invisible to EAS regardless of being present on disk locally,
# so a cloud build would silently produce an app Firebase can't initialize in.


